WEBVTT

00:17.142 --> 00:18.143
What?

00:45.920 --> 00:48.131
This is just a screen.

02:47.041 --> 02:49.127
These images are computer-generated.

02:49.210 --> 02:50.879
Computer-generated?

02:50.962 --> 02:51.963
All of this?

03:42.472 --> 03:44.349
- Welcome home.
- I'm back!

03:44.432 --> 03:46.684
- Here, I got this.
- Thanks.

03:47.435 --> 03:49.312
Oh! I'm starving!

04:43.783 --> 04:44.867
Usagi?

04:48.037 --> 04:49.789
Arisu…

05:01.634 --> 05:03.511
I missed you.

05:04.387 --> 05:05.847
So much.

05:08.349 --> 05:09.726
I'm sorry.

05:18.526 --> 05:19.694
Let's go home.

05:23.323 --> 05:24.824
Okay. Yeah.

05:26.993 --> 05:28.911
Sorry.

06:09.744 --> 06:10.870
It's you!

06:11.662 --> 06:12.789
Whoa! Easy!

06:12.872 --> 06:14.374
Why are you with Usagi?

06:14.457 --> 06:16.000
- Stop it!
- You killed her!

06:16.084 --> 06:17.877
- All this is your fault!
- Calm down!

06:17.960 --> 06:19.170
- Come on!
- Arisu, stop it!

06:19.253 --> 06:20.213
- Wait!
- Ryuji?

06:20.296 --> 06:24.675
- Ryuji, are you all right?
- Hold on. There you go.

06:27.220 --> 06:29.472
He's been fighting by my side
this whole time.

06:29.555 --> 06:30.515
Usagi…

06:30.598 --> 06:33.810
If he hadn't been there,
I wouldn't have made it this far.

06:34.811 --> 06:37.355
- But what he did is--
- What he did is save my life!

06:38.106 --> 06:40.358
What he did is bring us back together.

06:50.827 --> 06:53.579
Registration is now closed.

06:54.705 --> 06:57.750
Ten participants confirmed.

06:58.334 --> 07:00.044
Ten participants?

07:01.170 --> 07:03.339
But there are only nine of us here.

07:03.840 --> 07:05.633
What do you think it means?

07:06.759 --> 07:09.303
- A child.
- Huh?

07:12.306 --> 07:13.641
A child.

07:14.851 --> 07:16.185
What?

07:20.064 --> 07:22.442
The doctor said you're pregnant, Usagi.

07:25.862 --> 07:28.614
I… I'm pregnant?

07:30.450 --> 07:32.034
You're carrying our baby.

07:36.539 --> 07:37.540
Oh…

07:38.291 --> 07:40.918
So that's why it's ten people. The baby.

07:41.502 --> 07:43.754
Hey, kid, nice one!

07:43.838 --> 07:47.049
But… a child in this situation is…

07:55.850 --> 07:57.894
The game will now begin.

07:57.977 --> 07:59.604
It's about to start.

08:00.188 --> 08:03.649
Please put on your wristbands and collars.

08:18.122 --> 08:21.417
Game. Possible Futures.

09:49.839 --> 09:51.132
Game rules.

09:53.384 --> 09:56.095
There are a total of 25 rooms,

09:56.178 --> 09:58.264
arranged in five vertical columns

09:58.347 --> 10:00.808
and five horizontal rows.

10:00.891 --> 10:03.352
Each round, players must roll the dice

10:03.436 --> 10:06.480
found on the platform
in the center of the room.

10:06.564 --> 10:11.193
The resulting number determines how many
people can advance to the next chamber.

10:11.277 --> 10:13.988
Repeat until you reach the exit.

10:14.071 --> 10:17.116
You have a maximum of 15 rounds.

10:17.199 --> 10:18.409
EXIT

10:20.161 --> 10:25.708
However, those players who do not
advance because of the dice roll

10:25.791 --> 10:27.627
cannot move.

10:28.628 --> 10:32.131
A lockdown will activate,
forcing the player to stay.

10:32.214 --> 10:33.507
FORCED STAY

10:34.634 --> 10:36.677
To lift the lockdown,

10:36.761 --> 10:42.725
two players must use their wristbands
on either side of the locked room.

10:44.560 --> 10:46.520
UNLOCKED

10:46.604 --> 10:50.483
Each player has been allocated 15 points.

10:53.527 --> 10:56.614
To pass from one chamber to another,

10:56.697 --> 11:01.952
one player must spend one point
and hold their wristband up to the door.

11:03.829 --> 11:07.166
If you wish to return
to the room you just left,

11:07.249 --> 11:12.046
you must wait for one round
before being allowed to do so.

11:12.129 --> 11:16.842
Regardless of whether you remain
in a chamber by choice or by force,

11:16.926 --> 11:20.888
one point will be deducted
from your total each round.

11:20.971 --> 11:26.310
If a player's points reach zero,
they will be eliminated.

11:28.437 --> 11:34.527
The walls of each chamber will display
images of your possible future.

11:35.695 --> 11:39.281
The future you choose
from among those images

11:39.365 --> 11:43.285
will become your reality
once you reach the exit.

11:46.914 --> 11:49.125
We get to choose our own future…

11:51.544 --> 11:56.632
THE FUTURE THAT WILL COME TO PASS

11:57.508 --> 12:00.511
Proceed according to the dice roll

12:00.594 --> 12:04.557
and choose your future
as you search for the exit.

12:05.766 --> 12:09.562
Maybe the best strategy would be
to team up and work together.

12:14.400 --> 12:16.235
Hey, you two. What are your names?

12:21.907 --> 12:25.077
- I'm Sohta. This is my sister.
- Yuna.

12:25.828 --> 12:27.204
I'm Arisu.

12:28.873 --> 12:31.834
This is Sachiko, Rei,

12:32.460 --> 12:34.628
Tetsu, and Nobu.

12:36.756 --> 12:42.136
Begin. Roll the dice
and select the room you wish to enter.

12:42.219 --> 12:44.555
The time limit is three minutes.

13:00.946 --> 13:04.492
So the dice and the doors
are connected by color.

13:04.575 --> 13:08.662
All right!
Dice games are sorta my specialty.

13:09.413 --> 13:11.707
So then, you're a gambler too, are you?

13:12.958 --> 13:15.419
Round one. Start.

13:19.089 --> 13:22.092
Okay. Let's do this.

13:52.998 --> 13:55.251
Are these really visions of our future?

13:56.919 --> 13:59.713
All of this? No way.

14:07.805 --> 14:10.641
Here we go! Come on, baby! Yeah!

14:10.724 --> 14:13.644
- I hit the jackpot! Wow!
- You won!

14:16.397 --> 14:18.107
Thank you for the meal.

14:18.190 --> 14:19.441
What?

14:19.525 --> 14:20.860
No way, seriously?

14:25.531 --> 14:29.201
Look. I'm pretty sure
the future is different on each wall.

14:29.285 --> 14:31.495
Ah! Fuck this!

14:35.040 --> 14:36.000
Shit!

14:39.336 --> 14:42.673
So our futures change depending
on which door we pass through…

14:49.513 --> 14:50.973
Please, just read it, sir.

14:51.599 --> 14:55.644
This again, Matsuyama?
I've had about enough of this nonsense.

14:55.728 --> 14:58.606
No, Professor, please!
Just read the abstract! Anything!

14:58.689 --> 15:01.400
If I quit my research now,
it'll be all for nothing!

15:07.907 --> 15:12.745
No one's going to take this seriously.
Least of all the academic world.

15:13.746 --> 15:15.539
At least read a couple of pages, please.

15:16.957 --> 15:19.752
Maybe a magazine on the occult
would be more suitable?

15:37.645 --> 15:39.730
Over here! Look at Mommy!

15:39.813 --> 15:41.231
Smile!

15:42.399 --> 15:43.817
Beautiful day, too.

15:43.901 --> 15:46.111
Oh yeah, isn't it perfect?

15:47.196 --> 15:49.406
I don't know about you guys,

15:49.490 --> 15:51.825
but if that's the future, I choose blue.

15:53.077 --> 15:54.328
Me too.

15:55.287 --> 15:59.249
But we can't all go through.
Only seven of us are allowed.

16:00.042 --> 16:02.086
Why doesn't one person take yellow?

16:04.546 --> 16:06.465
- Yeah!
- Nice shot, Hida!

16:06.548 --> 16:07.925
All right!

16:08.842 --> 16:11.261
From what I see, yellow looks okay.

16:12.179 --> 16:15.641
No. We should probably try
to minimize wasting points.

16:15.724 --> 16:17.977
I'm pretty sure
that's the key to the game.

16:18.686 --> 16:19.812
So we stick together.

16:19.895 --> 16:21.855
We move through
as a group if we can, right?

16:23.899 --> 16:27.111
Yeah… We can't all go through
blue, so let's split into two groups

16:27.194 --> 16:29.196
and take the doors
with the largest numbers.

16:30.447 --> 16:34.702
Sohta and Yuna.
You two will be on a team with Rei.

16:36.537 --> 16:37.705
I want you three…

16:40.666 --> 16:43.711
to go to the room east of here, D3.

16:43.794 --> 16:46.755
The rest of us will go north, to C2.

16:46.839 --> 16:50.926
That way we can all meet up again
to the northeast, in D2.

16:51.552 --> 16:52.928
D3.

16:53.012 --> 16:55.389
That's great!

16:55.472 --> 16:57.683
- Yuna? Yuna?
- Ken? Is that you?

16:57.766 --> 16:59.351
I didn't even see you come in!

16:59.435 --> 17:00.936
This is my brother.

17:01.020 --> 17:03.480
- Ken is a classmate from university.
- We can do that.

17:03.564 --> 17:04.898
- Hi, I'm Ken.
- Hey there.

17:04.982 --> 17:07.192
Plus, the red door isn't a problem for us.

17:07.276 --> 17:08.235
See you!

17:08.318 --> 17:11.113
One minute remaining.

17:12.573 --> 17:14.950
- So that's the plan.
- Let's go.

17:15.034 --> 17:17.369
You all trust this guy,
no questions asked?

17:20.330 --> 17:22.624
If you don't like his plan,
try a different door.

17:34.678 --> 17:38.557
Please hold your wristbands
up to your chosen door

17:38.640 --> 17:41.226
to proceed to the next room.

17:44.563 --> 17:46.356
Let's do it. It's time.

18:00.037 --> 18:01.371
We'll see you guys in D2.

18:01.455 --> 18:02.664
Okay.

18:17.262 --> 18:18.764
I'm Rei Morikage.

18:18.847 --> 18:19.848
RÉSUMÉ
REI MORIKAGE

18:19.932 --> 18:23.769
I've loved anime ever since I was a kid
and… that inspires my drawings.

18:24.353 --> 18:26.647
How quickly are you able to draw?

18:27.147 --> 18:31.401
At the moment, it takes me
around three days to fill a page.

18:34.488 --> 18:37.908
C2 is a minus one point room.

18:37.991 --> 18:41.578
Please select the player
whose point will be deducted.

18:41.662 --> 18:43.580
What do they mean, "minus one point?"

18:43.664 --> 18:47.126
It means that some of these rooms
can remove points from us.

18:47.835 --> 18:50.379
But we won't know how many points
until we're already in.

18:50.462 --> 18:52.422
Which complicates things.

18:53.006 --> 18:56.969
We took from Arisu's points last time,
so now we can take from mine.

19:02.307 --> 19:05.477
Round two. Start.

19:13.569 --> 19:19.283
Now, roll the dice and select
the room you wish to enter.

19:20.701 --> 19:23.370
We can't go back the way we came
without waiting a round.

19:23.453 --> 19:27.082
There are three rooms we can enter.
That's why there are three dice.

19:27.166 --> 19:29.543
Okay! Stand aside.

19:35.883 --> 19:38.594
Three, one, five?

19:51.565 --> 19:54.026
If this shows the future we're gonna face,

19:54.610 --> 19:57.529
then I wanna choose the blue door again.

19:57.613 --> 19:59.323
MOVIE TICKET
EVERYBODY LOVES FAMILY!

19:59.406 --> 20:02.534
- We should do this more often.
- I've been wanting to see this.

20:02.618 --> 20:03.911
Huh.

20:06.538 --> 20:08.498
CLASS 1 ARCHITECT
DESIGN DRAWING EXAM

20:10.584 --> 20:11.460
Huh?

20:12.461 --> 20:14.963
You're going to study
to become an architect?

20:17.633 --> 20:18.592
What?

20:21.470 --> 20:24.264
If you encountered bullying among
your students, what would you do?

20:24.348 --> 20:26.391
Mr. Hida? What do you think?

20:26.475 --> 20:30.270
- Sir, I would take a measured approach.
- This future could really be mine?

20:30.354 --> 20:31.939
I'd listen to both sides.

20:32.022 --> 20:34.191
I don't wanna choose the red door.

20:42.115 --> 20:45.577
Hey. There's a seminar
you might like. Interested?

20:45.661 --> 20:46.745
SKILL DEVELOPMENT SEMINAR

20:46.828 --> 20:47.829
Ah, no, I'll pass.

20:47.913 --> 20:50.582
- I don't have the time.
- But it's like investing in your future!

20:50.666 --> 20:52.668
Time well spent, don't you think?

20:52.751 --> 20:54.753
At least give it a chance.

20:56.672 --> 20:58.340
Would you write your name, please.

20:58.924 --> 21:00.884
All right, thank you.

21:00.968 --> 21:03.053
Please take a seat in any available chair.

21:03.136 --> 21:06.765
D2, where we're planning
to meet up, is behind the red door.

21:07.808 --> 21:09.393
So I'll take that one.

21:09.476 --> 21:12.646
I'll meet up with Rei
and the rest of the group.

21:13.689 --> 21:14.898
Then I'm going with you.

21:16.858 --> 21:19.820
Then as for the rest of you,
go through the blue one, okay?

21:19.903 --> 21:21.446
To room C1.

21:21.530 --> 21:25.492
Well done, Matsuyama!
The research funding you were hoping for!

21:25.575 --> 21:28.704
- Is this really happening?
- It is. Congratulations.

21:28.787 --> 21:30.163
Thank you so much.

21:32.874 --> 21:34.418
I'll meet up with you later.

21:39.756 --> 21:42.426
Well…

21:43.760 --> 21:44.594
Let's go.

21:52.227 --> 21:54.771
TO: YUZUHA ARISU

21:54.855 --> 21:57.941
THANK YOU FOR THE OTHER DAY
CAN WE MEET?

22:02.612 --> 22:05.365
I'm getting a weird feeling
from this game.

22:06.742 --> 22:10.829
Is it actually reading all our minds?
Does it know what we're thinking?

22:21.048 --> 22:21.923
All twos.

22:35.437 --> 22:38.231
I'm going to head north to room D2.

22:38.315 --> 22:40.901
Ideally, I'd like
the three of us to go together.

22:41.860 --> 22:43.987
But we have to split into two groups.

22:44.780 --> 22:46.406
That sounds good.

22:46.948 --> 22:51.203
The two of us will go… east, to E3.

22:51.286 --> 22:52.204
Right.

22:52.704 --> 22:54.623
JOB OFFER CONFIRMATION

22:54.706 --> 22:57.042
Oh my gosh!

23:01.922 --> 23:05.258
- Whoa, this is so good!
- Hey, are you listening to me?

23:11.056 --> 23:14.810
Rei. Let's meet up in room D2, as planned.

23:14.893 --> 23:16.645
Roger that.

23:27.739 --> 23:29.616
- All right.
- That's a relief.

23:29.699 --> 23:30.951
Yeah.

23:31.034 --> 23:33.453
Round three. Start.

23:34.871 --> 23:36.331
Huh?

23:36.415 --> 23:37.833
One and two?

23:49.886 --> 23:54.057
Usagi counts as two people here.
So she has to go to D1.

23:54.975 --> 23:57.602
And only one of us can go through to E2.

23:57.686 --> 24:00.730
That means no matter what we do,
someone has to stay behind.

24:03.442 --> 24:04.609
Attention, everyone.

24:04.693 --> 24:07.529
This is Morikage.
She'll be starting today.

24:07.612 --> 24:09.739
I look forward to working with you all.

24:09.823 --> 24:11.074
I'm Rei Morikage.

24:11.158 --> 24:13.285
It's nice to meet you.

24:14.911 --> 24:17.205
Well, I guess it is what it is.

24:17.706 --> 24:19.708
I'd like you to begin with this cut.

24:19.791 --> 24:21.543
I'll stay behind this time.

24:21.626 --> 24:22.794
What?

24:23.587 --> 24:25.088
You have a baby who needs you.

24:25.755 --> 24:27.507
- But…
- Rei…

24:28.216 --> 24:30.469
I owe you one for the zombie thing.

24:33.889 --> 24:35.015
Hmm.

24:39.895 --> 24:42.981
Usagi, you meet up
with Sachiko and the others.

24:44.900 --> 24:46.568
Sachiko, can you hear me?

24:52.240 --> 24:53.825
Yeah, I can hear you.

24:54.743 --> 24:56.786
How many people can go on to D1?

24:57.329 --> 25:00.665
- Who gives a rat's ass…
- Four. We all can.

25:01.500 --> 25:04.002
- But when you drink…
- That's great. Then do it.

25:04.085 --> 25:06.880
- All of you go east to D1.
- All you ever do is nag.

25:06.963 --> 25:09.799
- Would you keep your voice down?
- I want you to meet Usagi there.

25:09.883 --> 25:12.219
Oh, sorry, I wouldn't wanna be heard…

25:12.302 --> 25:15.180
- That's not what I meant.
- Who cares what you meant?

25:16.348 --> 25:17.349
Got it.

25:19.351 --> 25:23.230
Sohta, Yuna,
could you stay where you are for a minute?

25:24.356 --> 25:28.151
Usagi and I will move this round.
And Rei's staying behind.

25:29.319 --> 25:32.155
I want you to go back to D3 next round.

25:32.781 --> 25:35.534
We can lift Rei's lockdown
and get her out.

25:36.451 --> 25:38.995
Afterward, we'll meet up in E3.

25:39.579 --> 25:41.289
It's probably best if we coordinate.

25:41.373 --> 25:43.667
We should stay? Okay, will do.

25:50.382 --> 25:52.801
All right, let's all go to D1 together.

25:52.884 --> 25:56.471
Are you suggesting that because
Arisu said we should move as a group?

25:57.889 --> 25:59.766
- Well, I mean--
- Listen.

25:59.849 --> 26:02.185
We're supposed to be looking for the exit.

26:02.269 --> 26:05.230
If we split up,
we might be able to find it faster.

26:06.356 --> 26:07.607
And besides,

26:09.067 --> 26:11.695
shouldn't we get to know
our futures a little better?

26:30.672 --> 26:34.384
Mr. Matsuyama!
These numbers are incredible.

26:34.467 --> 26:38.138
I think this data is enough to prove
your hypothesis, Mr. Matsuyama.

26:38.221 --> 26:40.473
You did it! You did it!

26:41.850 --> 26:46.438
And you get to sell these bottles
for not one, but 3,000 apiece!

26:47.147 --> 26:50.066
Listen, if you don't like it,
the door is right there.

26:50.150 --> 26:52.027
Only those who are super committed

26:52.110 --> 26:54.404
to becoming entrepreneurs
should come with me.

26:54.487 --> 26:56.156
You. Why are you here?

26:56.239 --> 26:58.700
I'm here to develop my potential!

26:58.783 --> 27:00.535
Very good, that's right!

27:00.619 --> 27:05.582
In that case, your challenge will be
to sell this water for 30,000 a bottle.

27:06.625 --> 27:09.127
You understand
why you need to sell it, don't you?

27:09.210 --> 27:10.629
TRUE AWAKENING
LUCKY WATER

27:10.712 --> 27:13.131
- Excuse me.
- Uh… no thanks.

27:14.090 --> 27:15.967
No, thank you.

27:16.051 --> 27:17.260
It's impossible!

27:17.344 --> 27:19.554
- I need my money back!
- Are you serious?

27:19.638 --> 27:24.309
It's all here in black and white, kid!
Absolutely no returns!

27:26.144 --> 27:27.604
- Excuse me.
- What?

27:27.687 --> 27:29.189
I'm so sorry, sir.

27:29.272 --> 27:32.359
- He's drunk.
- Why are you apologizing, bitch?

27:32.442 --> 27:34.152
- I asked you a question.
- Stop!

27:34.235 --> 27:36.738
- What are you doing?
- Sir! You can't do that!

27:36.821 --> 27:38.490
REJECTION LETTER

27:42.994 --> 27:45.246
- You're hired.
- I am?

27:45.747 --> 27:47.582
We look forward to working with you.

27:47.666 --> 27:49.292
Thank you so much.

27:49.376 --> 27:52.379
- Thank you for being here.
- I really appreciate it.

27:58.093 --> 28:01.179
If it were me, I would put the exit
as far away as I could.

28:01.262 --> 28:03.348
It makes sense for it to be in a corner.

28:04.140 --> 28:06.226
It's a good point.

28:06.309 --> 28:08.770
It might be worth trying once, at least.

28:10.105 --> 28:11.106
All right.

28:12.565 --> 28:16.319
Fine. We'll check the corner rooms
by splitting into two groups.

28:16.403 --> 28:19.823
But also,
Arisu's plan is too good to ignore.

28:19.906 --> 28:23.910
So we'll do both.
Let's you and I go through this door.

28:24.411 --> 28:27.497
That way, I can meet up with Usagi,
and you can try your plan,

28:27.580 --> 28:29.541
and hopefully, you find the exit.

28:30.625 --> 28:31.793
Yeah, all right.

28:33.712 --> 28:37.298
And we'll go this way. To B1.

28:38.341 --> 28:39.426
Sound good?

28:40.677 --> 28:41.803
Uh, yeah.

28:57.444 --> 28:59.654
- We should break up.
- What?

28:59.738 --> 29:01.406
I don't love you anymore.

29:02.407 --> 29:04.033
Did I do something wrong, Ken?

29:04.117 --> 29:05.869
- Did I hurt you?
- Look, Sohta.

29:05.952 --> 29:06.995
I'm sorry.

29:07.078 --> 29:09.247
No, wait! Please, Ken! Please!

29:11.207 --> 29:12.375
Please stay!

29:13.251 --> 29:16.212
We're… well, we're getting married!

29:17.046 --> 29:19.090
We're hoping for your blessing.

29:20.049 --> 29:21.468
Yeah! Of course.

29:21.551 --> 29:23.386
- Yeah!
- Congratulations, sis.

29:23.470 --> 29:25.555
- Thank you.
- Thank you so much.

29:51.498 --> 29:54.000
Whoa, that lake is so freaking big. Look!

29:54.083 --> 29:56.711
- Ah!
- Yuna, come on, it's a dam, not a lake.

29:56.795 --> 29:57.754
That's a dam?

29:57.837 --> 30:00.381
- It's a reservoir created by a dam.
- Come on, Dad!

30:00.965 --> 30:02.550
Well, that makes Yuna half-right!

30:02.634 --> 30:04.844
You see, I'm half-right!

30:04.928 --> 30:06.554
You're pretty excited today.

30:06.638 --> 30:07.972
Well, yeah, duh!

30:08.056 --> 30:11.100
It's been so long since
we've had a vacation, all four of us!

30:11.184 --> 30:12.268
- I love it!
- Me too!

30:28.827 --> 30:31.120
We did everything we could.

30:32.747 --> 30:36.334
I'm so sorry. Your parents
didn't make it out of surgery.

31:50.575 --> 31:54.120
Hold your wristband up to your chosen door

31:54.203 --> 31:57.206
and proceed to the next room.

32:03.129 --> 32:05.924
Sohta, are you sure?

32:23.524 --> 32:24.984
Lockdown.

32:27.862 --> 32:29.739
You are completely useless!

32:34.994 --> 32:35.912
No!

32:38.790 --> 32:40.792
You are completely useless!

32:42.043 --> 32:43.920
What is this?

32:45.046 --> 32:45.922
1 ROOM

32:46.005 --> 32:49.342
Point deduction confirmed.

32:49.425 --> 32:52.053
Round four. Start.

32:53.096 --> 32:54.931
- Let me roll the dice.
- Mm-hm.

33:19.956 --> 33:22.709
If we wanna get to the corner,
we need to head west.

33:23.209 --> 33:24.794
But only one person can go.

33:26.754 --> 33:29.298
I don't think
it's a good idea to split up.

33:30.508 --> 33:31.759
Let's try B2.

33:31.843 --> 33:33.386
- You did it!
- Uh…

33:33.469 --> 33:35.763
- You got the job!
- Nobu, you got the job?

33:35.847 --> 33:37.682
- Congrats, man!
- That's amazing!

33:37.765 --> 33:39.434
- Great job, dude!
- Nobu.

33:39.517 --> 33:41.477
Nice work!

33:41.561 --> 33:42.895
Did you hear me?

33:43.438 --> 33:45.940
- Yeah.
- You did it! You got the job!

33:46.024 --> 33:48.026
Nobu, you got the job? Congrats, man!

33:48.109 --> 33:49.485
That's amazing! Great job!

33:49.569 --> 33:52.697
Let's stay here
so we can release Rei from lockdown.

33:54.490 --> 33:56.743
I'm still going next door
to the corner room.

33:56.826 --> 33:58.369
And if it's a trap? What then?

33:58.453 --> 34:00.079
I've still got 15 points.

34:00.163 --> 34:01.998
I'll be fine.

34:05.334 --> 34:06.335
Sohta?

34:07.003 --> 34:08.880
I need to know what you rolled.

34:15.970 --> 34:16.971
Sohta?

34:18.306 --> 34:20.767
Sohta? Yuna?

34:21.768 --> 34:23.770
You're in E3 now, right?

34:24.353 --> 34:27.774
Can you move to D3?
We need to get Rei out.

34:29.025 --> 34:30.109
Understood.

34:31.527 --> 34:32.737
Are you sure?

34:35.615 --> 34:36.699
Hey, look.

34:42.872 --> 34:45.166
The green door leads to a corner room.

34:46.250 --> 34:47.960
And maybe that's where the exit is.

34:48.586 --> 34:49.754
I don't know Arisu well,

34:49.837 --> 34:53.341
but if he had to choose between
saving us or Usagi,

34:53.424 --> 34:55.468
no way he's giving up her or his kid.

34:59.097 --> 35:00.973
We need to make sure that's our future.

35:01.808 --> 35:04.268
We need to move forward for Mom and Dad.

35:15.238 --> 35:16.280
Let's go.

35:17.240 --> 35:18.199
Mm-hm.

35:22.703 --> 35:23.788
Here we go.

35:31.003 --> 35:31.838
Rei?

35:32.588 --> 35:33.422
You okay?

35:33.506 --> 35:36.259
I'm going crazy in here! Hurry up, please!

35:36.342 --> 35:39.095
Sohta and his sister
are heading to D3 now.

35:39.178 --> 35:40.888
They'll get you out.

35:43.808 --> 35:45.143
Help me, please!

36:04.370 --> 36:06.414
- Congrats, man!
- Great job!

36:07.373 --> 36:08.291
Hey!

36:09.625 --> 36:11.169
Let's go, come on.

36:12.753 --> 36:14.672
I'll use my points for the door.

37:03.262 --> 37:06.515
To Nobu! The kid
who can sell even the weirdest water!

37:07.558 --> 37:10.561
Drink this and I'll buy one! Go on!

37:10.645 --> 37:15.483
Chug! Chug! Chug! Chug!
Chug! Chug! Chug! Chug! Chug!

37:15.566 --> 37:19.028
- Come on man, you got it! Chug!
- Chug! Chug! Chug! Chug!

37:19.111 --> 37:21.781
- More! Get this guy another!
- Keep going!

37:21.864 --> 37:23.574
Chug! Chug! Chug! Chug!

37:23.658 --> 37:26.494
- Why do…
- Nobu's got a drink 

37:26.577 --> 37:29.163
- Yeah!
- Got his glass, filled it up!

37:29.247 --> 37:31.958
- Keep going!
- Drink it down, drink it down 

37:32.041 --> 37:34.335
Drink it down 

37:34.418 --> 37:36.837
No more, please! I'm dying.

37:36.921 --> 37:38.756
He says he doesn't wanna drink!

37:38.839 --> 37:40.925
Drink it down, drink, drink it down 

37:41.008 --> 37:43.010
Drink, drink it down
Drink, drink it down 

37:43.094 --> 37:44.762
- Drink it down!
- Drink! Drink!

37:44.845 --> 37:47.265
Drink it down, ya gotta drink it down

37:47.348 --> 37:50.559
Ya gotta drink it down
Ya gotta drink, drink 

37:50.643 --> 37:52.478
Drink it down, ya gotta drink--

37:52.561 --> 37:54.313
Whoa!

37:54.397 --> 37:55.773
- So gross!
- Crazy!

37:55.856 --> 37:57.275
Sorry, I…

37:57.358 --> 37:59.360
Here!

38:00.695 --> 38:03.197
- Eat shit!
- Eat shit! Eat shit!

38:03.281 --> 38:05.241
Eat shit! Eat shit! Eat shit!

38:05.324 --> 38:06.534
Eat shit! Eat shit…

38:06.617 --> 38:09.620
I'm sorry. I'm leaving!

38:09.704 --> 38:11.414
Hey!

38:14.000 --> 38:15.293
Nobu!

38:16.043 --> 38:18.129
What the hell is going on?

38:30.057 --> 38:32.893
So I guess it's just me now…

38:33.394 --> 38:34.478
6 ROOM
NOBUAKI HIDA: 13

38:34.562 --> 38:38.649
A1 is a minus six point room.

38:38.733 --> 38:39.775
Are you kidding?

38:45.197 --> 38:46.615
It's not the exit.

38:47.158 --> 38:50.328
And there's only one other door,
because it's the corner room!

38:50.911 --> 38:55.041
E5 is a minus four point room.

38:55.124 --> 38:56.208
No…

38:57.668 --> 38:59.503
4 ROOM
SOHTA ITSUKI: 13, YUNA ITSUKI: 14

38:59.587 --> 39:00.671
Damn it.

39:01.714 --> 39:03.049
We'll use my points.

39:03.132 --> 39:04.592
But…

39:05.634 --> 39:08.471
Point deduction confirmed.

39:11.057 --> 39:11.932
It's okay.

39:13.934 --> 39:16.604
Round five. Start.

39:21.567 --> 39:23.736
Rei. Are you out?

39:24.737 --> 39:28.949
No, I'm still trapped!
And I lost another point!

39:29.033 --> 39:29.909
What?

39:34.955 --> 39:37.249
- Come on in!
- Thanks! Here, for you!

39:37.333 --> 39:38.876
- A housewarming gift.
- What is it?

39:38.959 --> 39:40.544
- You shouldn't have!
- Ta-da!

39:40.628 --> 39:42.171
- Sohta? Yuna?
- It's cute.

39:42.254 --> 39:45.091
- Where are you?
- Sohta, you've got great taste!

39:47.009 --> 39:48.344
Oh, this is far from over!

39:48.427 --> 39:50.554
- Sohta? Yuna!
- You are completely useless!

39:52.390 --> 39:54.558
Sohta! Yuna!

40:01.315 --> 40:03.317
Oh, this is far from over!

40:03.401 --> 40:05.611
- You are completely useless!
- That's it.

40:06.195 --> 40:07.863
They made their choice.

40:08.447 --> 40:10.699
Instead of helping each other out,

40:11.575 --> 40:14.036
humans will choose
whatever's best for them.

40:14.537 --> 40:16.038
We're all selfish.

40:17.206 --> 40:18.666
Get out! Just get out!

40:18.749 --> 40:21.001
Wait! Just let me explain! Please!

40:21.085 --> 40:23.087
FROM: MOM
PLEASE JUST CALL ONCE

40:27.967 --> 40:29.718
Oh, this is far from over!

40:29.802 --> 40:32.179
You are completely useless!

40:32.263 --> 40:35.808
Come to think of it… how is Mom?

40:35.891 --> 40:37.393
I wonder how she is.

40:41.647 --> 40:42.982
Oh shit.

40:48.487 --> 40:49.780
Gimme another bag.

40:49.864 --> 40:52.533
And this stuff's even better,
man, trust me.

41:15.347 --> 41:16.724
No freaking way.

41:18.851 --> 41:21.353
Didn't it show me throwing it all away?

41:27.401 --> 41:29.069
No!

41:29.153 --> 41:30.154
Ah, shit!

41:30.237 --> 41:31.655
Help me!

41:32.907 --> 41:34.283
Help me!

41:45.961 --> 41:47.213
Mom?

41:47.296 --> 41:48.923
What happened?

41:49.006 --> 41:51.675
Your mother suffered
a cerebral hemorrhage.

41:51.759 --> 41:52.843
Mom, no…

41:53.844 --> 41:55.054
Nobu?

41:57.640 --> 42:01.227
Even if she recovers, your mother
will need around-the-clock care.

42:01.310 --> 42:03.062
No, it can't be true.

42:14.865 --> 42:16.534
Usagi.

42:17.284 --> 42:22.248
I'm going to D3 next to get Rei out
of lockdown. I need you to stay put.

42:22.331 --> 42:23.332
Got it.

42:24.500 --> 42:25.501
Ryuji.

42:26.377 --> 42:29.171
Can you hear me? Anything over there?

42:30.047 --> 42:32.925
E1 was a minus one point room, that's all.

42:34.134 --> 42:36.220
- And no exit?
- No.

42:52.027 --> 42:53.487
No… no way…

42:54.905 --> 42:56.115
They're lying!

42:58.993 --> 42:59.868
Huh?

43:05.457 --> 43:06.792
No way…

43:08.919 --> 43:10.087
No way…

43:11.130 --> 43:12.381
Impossible.

43:13.340 --> 43:14.550
No way!

43:18.887 --> 43:20.264
Mom, please…

43:22.224 --> 43:24.143
It's all my fault.

43:28.689 --> 43:31.025
I'm… I'm… I'm sorry.

44:08.395 --> 44:10.397
Oh, this is far from over!

44:11.231 --> 44:12.483
D2 UNLOCKED

44:12.566 --> 44:14.276
Huh?

44:16.945 --> 44:20.366
Room D2 has been unlocked.

44:23.577 --> 44:26.372
Rei. You can leave now.

44:27.790 --> 44:29.124
Let's meet up next round.

44:31.710 --> 44:32.670
All right.

44:33.879 --> 44:34.963
Thank you.

44:54.024 --> 44:55.234
4 ROOM
TETSU SHIMAZAKI: 12

44:55.317 --> 44:59.446
B3 is a minus four point room.

44:59.530 --> 45:01.532
Minus four?

45:02.991 --> 45:05.994
Point deduction confirmed.

45:11.834 --> 45:13.961
- Tetsu? Nobu?
- Huh?

45:15.754 --> 45:18.340
Nobu! Are you there?

45:21.635 --> 45:25.597
Hey, don't worry. It's all right.
I still have some points left.

45:27.891 --> 45:30.769
Point deduction confirmed.

45:42.573 --> 45:44.032
Ah! Fuck!

45:46.493 --> 45:48.704
Fuckin' hell!

45:51.999 --> 45:53.876
Hey. Sorry I'm late.

45:57.963 --> 45:59.423
That's okay.

46:02.718 --> 46:03.927
Yukiko?

46:10.225 --> 46:11.435
Hey, Yukiko.

46:11.518 --> 46:12.519
Yeah?

46:13.020 --> 46:15.272
Wanna go to the aquarium
for our anniversary?

46:15.939 --> 46:17.107
Why there?

46:19.443 --> 46:20.861
Because I've never been.

46:20.944 --> 46:22.946
What? Not even as a kid?

46:23.447 --> 46:25.491
Nope.

46:25.574 --> 46:27.910
Sure!

46:31.705 --> 46:34.541
Long time no see. You look good.

47:07.491 --> 47:09.159
Would you look at you?

47:09.243 --> 47:10.619
Wow!

47:11.578 --> 47:14.373
Yeah, I'm working
at a construction company.

47:14.915 --> 47:16.458
I can change.

47:16.542 --> 47:18.669
What? Really?

47:20.420 --> 47:22.756
I swear I can change, Yukiko.

47:44.069 --> 47:45.904
No!

48:04.256 --> 48:05.757
- Welcome.
- Welcome.

48:05.841 --> 48:07.384
Welcome.

48:13.891 --> 48:15.392
I've been waiting for you.

48:15.475 --> 48:16.935
Sorry I'm late.

48:17.019 --> 48:18.812
I didn't think you would show up.

48:18.896 --> 48:21.398
What? As if I would miss this!

48:22.816 --> 48:24.985
- Hey.
- Hmm?

48:25.485 --> 48:27.029
Would you like me to build you a house?

48:27.112 --> 48:28.155
For me?

48:28.238 --> 48:30.324
Uh-huh. What kind would you want?

48:30.407 --> 48:33.327
- Hm… a big house.
- Yeah?

48:33.410 --> 48:34.828
- Lots of space.
- Uh-huh.

50:34.072 --> 50:38.452
A3 is a minus eight point room.

50:42.497 --> 50:46.334
Your points total is now zero.

50:47.127 --> 50:48.295
Game over.

50:54.301 --> 50:55.761
I'm done.

51:01.224 --> 51:03.935
Police. We have a warrant
to search the premises.

51:06.813 --> 51:07.898
Found it!

51:17.783 --> 51:19.785
- What are you doing?
- Nothing.

51:19.868 --> 51:21.870
- I'm fine.
- I knew it. I knew you wouldn't change!

51:21.953 --> 51:23.455
Get off me!

51:24.039 --> 51:27.042
You're the one who doesn't trust me!

51:27.125 --> 51:29.377
I did trust you!

51:29.461 --> 51:31.171
I trusted you!

51:31.254 --> 51:33.924
That's why it hurts so much!

51:40.347 --> 51:42.766
Okay. I'm done.

52:04.037 --> 52:06.456
This is my future, I guess. Huh.

52:20.554 --> 52:22.597
It's my fault. I did this.

52:42.325 --> 52:43.326
Nobu?

52:50.542 --> 52:52.627
Why don't you tell me what happened?

52:55.338 --> 52:57.007
Talk to me, please.

52:58.717 --> 53:00.010
Don't come in.

53:01.720 --> 53:04.806
Just tell me. I'm on your side.

53:22.574 --> 53:25.785
No matter what happens, keep living.

54:03.114 --> 54:04.366
I will, Mom.

54:06.868 --> 54:08.578
I promise I will.

54:48.451 --> 54:51.079
- Would you like to say a few words?
- Sure. Thank you.

54:51.162 --> 54:54.666
I've just been appointed here.
My name is Nobuaki Hida.

54:55.166 --> 54:57.335
And my mother's a teacher.

54:58.003 --> 55:01.381
She's the one who inspired
me to be one too.

55:02.173 --> 55:05.927
I'm looking forward to working
with all of you. Thank you.

55:11.516 --> 55:13.518
NOBUAKI HIDA

55:14.686 --> 55:18.148
Hold your wristband up to your chosen door

55:18.231 --> 55:21.109
and proceed to the next room.

55:22.319 --> 55:24.154
I need to go find Tetsu.

55:46.051 --> 55:47.260
Nobu?

55:48.845 --> 55:51.681
Nobu, tell us where you are. Nobu?

55:52.807 --> 55:54.476
1 ROOM
NOBUAKI HIDA: 4

55:57.020 --> 55:58.104
Nobu?

55:59.189 --> 56:02.108
Huh? Yeah. Sachiko?

56:02.609 --> 56:04.069
Are you all right?

56:04.736 --> 56:06.988
I came back.

56:07.072 --> 56:09.074
I'm back in room B1.

56:09.157 --> 56:11.201
But Tetsu and I got separated.

56:11.993 --> 56:15.914
Did you go to the corner room,
A1? That might be the exit.

56:16.664 --> 56:18.917
Yeah. But there was nothing there.

56:19.000 --> 56:22.504
We're in C1.
We're right next to you, okay?

56:23.004 --> 56:25.924
We can meet up with you next round,
so stay where you are.

56:26.007 --> 56:27.801
- Sound good?
- Okay.

56:30.595 --> 56:33.681
Round seven. Start.

56:46.069 --> 56:47.862
Oh no…

56:48.738 --> 56:50.281
Only one each.

56:50.949 --> 56:52.742
We'll have to split up.

57:01.876 --> 57:04.838
Usagi. I'm in D3 now.

57:04.921 --> 57:06.965
I finally met up with Rei.

57:08.091 --> 57:10.635
If there's no exit in the A1 corner room,

57:10.718 --> 57:13.388
then A5 and E5 are
the corners we have left.

57:14.055 --> 57:16.057
The exit is probably in one of those.

57:16.933 --> 57:20.353
But first,
let's look for Sohta and the others.

57:20.437 --> 57:21.521
Got it.

57:33.616 --> 57:35.368
You wanna do another interview?

57:35.952 --> 57:37.245
I've been…

57:39.038 --> 57:41.624
well, compiling my research, actually.

57:41.708 --> 57:43.668
Near-death experiences?

57:45.336 --> 57:47.505
I didn't think my story
was that interesting.

57:47.589 --> 57:49.716
No, of course it is.

57:51.134 --> 57:53.928
Look, I wanna thank you.
Can I buy you dinner?

57:55.013 --> 57:57.348
Um, let me think about that.

58:12.822 --> 58:14.324
Come with me.

58:16.034 --> 58:17.785
We're going to the land of death.

58:47.065 --> 58:49.943
In the final game, I want you to kill her.

58:50.026 --> 58:52.320
Then your work here will be finished.

59:07.752 --> 59:12.173
If you kill Usagi,
I promise to grant your wish.

59:12.257 --> 59:16.010
I promise you will learn
about who governs the afterlife.

59:16.094 --> 59:19.347
I promise you will learn
about the land of the dead.

59:23.977 --> 59:25.645
Ryuji, are you there?

59:27.313 --> 59:29.232
Ryuji?

59:29.315 --> 59:31.776
- Ryuji!
- Hold your wristband up…

59:31.859 --> 59:33.361
Yeah, I hear you.

59:33.444 --> 59:36.197
- Proceed to the next room.
- We should meet back up.

59:36.781 --> 59:39.200
Make sure we meet up in B4.

59:43.162 --> 59:46.541
Oh! Sweet, thanks! Thanks so much.

01:00:14.861 --> 01:00:16.821
- Nobu!
- I'm so happy to see you!

01:00:16.904 --> 01:00:18.948
- Are you okay?
- Glad you're all right.

01:00:19.657 --> 01:00:24.078
B1 is a minus one point room.

01:00:24.162 --> 01:00:25.997
Better use my points here.

01:00:29.417 --> 01:00:31.502
We still need to find Tetsu!

01:00:32.420 --> 01:00:34.964
Tetsu? Tetsu.

01:00:35.632 --> 01:00:38.551
Tetsu? Can you hear us, Tetsu?

01:00:38.635 --> 01:00:39.636
Tetsu?

01:00:39.719 --> 01:00:42.430
Round eight. Start.

01:00:56.235 --> 01:00:57.362
Sohta!

01:00:58.071 --> 01:01:01.282
- Oh, wow!
- Wow! It is yummy!

01:01:15.004 --> 01:01:16.506
No!

01:01:16.589 --> 01:01:17.757
Come to Mommy!

01:01:28.184 --> 01:01:31.771
Hold your wristband up to your chosen door

01:01:31.854 --> 01:01:34.399
and proceed to the next room.

01:01:41.989 --> 01:01:44.033
Yuna.

01:01:44.117 --> 01:01:45.868
Sohta!

01:01:49.497 --> 01:01:50.456
Yuna?

01:01:52.250 --> 01:01:53.126
Yuna!

01:01:54.919 --> 01:01:57.672
Sohta! I can't get through.
It won't let me in!

01:01:58.464 --> 01:02:00.341
- Sohta!
- Yuna!

01:02:02.301 --> 01:02:06.848
- B4 is a minus two point room.
- What?

01:02:06.931 --> 01:02:08.224
2 ROOM

01:02:10.351 --> 01:02:13.813
Your points total is now zero.

01:02:15.440 --> 01:02:17.108
Game over.

01:03:19.212 --> 01:03:23.424
Sohta! Sohta! Sohta…

01:03:25.384 --> 01:03:27.470
Sohta. No, no…

01:03:27.553 --> 01:03:30.139
No, please. Please. I…

01:03:30.223 --> 01:03:31.766
I… I… 

01:03:31.849 --> 01:03:34.310
- Yuna.
- Please… Please, please…

01:03:34.393 --> 01:03:37.396
- This was a minus two room.
- No…

01:03:38.898 --> 01:03:41.442
What? No, no…

01:03:43.236 --> 01:03:44.362
No. No!

01:03:44.445 --> 01:03:47.323
- No, no, no…
- I'm so sorry.

01:03:47.406 --> 01:03:49.325
No, no…

01:03:49.951 --> 01:03:51.828
- I can't keep my promise to you.
- No!

01:03:52.870 --> 01:03:55.915
No! Sohta! Open the door!

01:03:55.998 --> 01:03:58.084
Someone, please let me in! Please!

01:03:58.167 --> 01:04:00.795
No! No!

01:04:00.878 --> 01:04:04.257
No! Please don't leave me! Please!

01:04:04.340 --> 01:04:06.551
Don't go! Please!

01:04:06.634 --> 01:04:09.762
No, no, no, please!

01:04:09.846 --> 01:04:12.473
Wait. Don't go, please…

01:04:13.474 --> 01:04:16.477
Please! No, please, please…

01:04:20.439 --> 01:04:22.567
No, please!

01:04:22.650 --> 01:04:24.777
Please… No! No!

01:04:24.861 --> 01:04:27.071
- Find happiness. I love you.
- No!

01:04:27.154 --> 01:04:29.115
Wait! Please don't go!

01:04:29.198 --> 01:04:32.994
Don't leave me! Sohta!
Sohta, don't go! Please!

01:04:33.077 --> 01:04:35.079
No! No!

01:04:35.162 --> 01:04:36.956
Please, no.

01:04:37.540 --> 01:04:39.834
No, no, no…

01:04:39.917 --> 01:04:42.211
Please… please…

01:05:30.509 --> 01:05:34.805
YUZUHA ARISU: 9, RYUJI MATSUYAMA: 7
NOBUAKI HIDA: 3, SACHIKO MAKINO: 11

01:05:34.889 --> 01:05:36.474
Sohta is…

01:05:38.351 --> 01:05:39.268
Yeah.

01:05:40.519 --> 01:05:42.563
I don't know where Tetsu is, either.

01:05:45.107 --> 01:05:46.484
Tetsu?

01:05:48.235 --> 01:05:49.528
Tetsu, are you there?

01:05:54.408 --> 01:05:56.494
It's because I left him behind.

01:05:57.244 --> 01:05:58.579
Behind?

01:05:59.747 --> 01:06:01.916
We don't know for sure that he died.

01:06:02.416 --> 01:06:04.794
He's just not answering you, that's all.

01:06:08.839 --> 01:06:11.008
B4 is a minus two room.

01:06:11.968 --> 01:06:12.843
Rei.

01:06:18.891 --> 01:06:22.937
I want you to go south.
Take Yuna and head to C5.

01:06:23.813 --> 01:06:25.356
Looking at the rounds,

01:06:25.439 --> 01:06:27.900
Yuna and her brother
must have passed through E5.

01:06:28.567 --> 01:06:33.781
If E5 wasn't the exit, that means
A5 is the only corner room left.

01:06:33.864 --> 01:06:34.824
Right.

01:06:35.783 --> 01:06:39.120
I'll meet up with everyone in B4,
and then we'll head to A5.

01:06:39.996 --> 01:06:43.207
It's the last corner room.
It has to be the exit.

01:06:56.804 --> 01:06:57.805
Yuna.

01:06:59.432 --> 01:07:01.559
You're gonna have
to go with Rei to the exit.

01:07:03.811 --> 01:07:06.480
Yuna. We have to go.

01:07:06.981 --> 01:07:09.483
Let's get going. Okay?

01:07:09.567 --> 01:07:11.527
Yuna.

01:07:11.610 --> 01:07:15.573
Hold your wristband up to your chosen door

01:07:15.656 --> 01:07:18.451
and proceed to the next room.

01:07:18.534 --> 01:07:20.161
Yuna, come on. Let's go.

01:07:42.058 --> 01:07:43.517
Sohta? Sohta!

01:07:43.601 --> 01:07:45.061
- Yuna!
- Yuna!

01:07:45.144 --> 01:07:47.438
You can't be in here!
You have to go with Rei!

01:07:47.521 --> 01:07:50.149
- Yuna! Come with me! Hurry!
- Yuna!

01:07:50.232 --> 01:07:52.234
- This door's gonna close!
- Get back!

01:07:55.780 --> 01:07:58.282
- The player left in this room…
- No!

01:07:58.365 --> 01:08:00.451
…will be under lockdown.

01:08:06.165 --> 01:08:10.252
B4 is a minus two point room.

01:08:10.836 --> 01:08:15.216
Please select the player
whose points will be deducted.

01:08:20.054 --> 01:08:22.765
Point deduction confirmed.

01:08:27.645 --> 01:08:31.732
B3 is a minus four point room.

01:08:31.816 --> 01:08:33.776
We're losing four points.

01:08:34.401 --> 01:08:36.445
We should deduct from my pool.

01:08:39.198 --> 01:08:42.034
Point deduction confirmed.

01:08:42.118 --> 01:08:45.579
Round ten. Start.

01:09:07.434 --> 01:09:09.103
Oh no…

01:09:16.443 --> 01:09:17.278
Usagi.

01:09:18.112 --> 01:09:19.572
How's it going over there?

01:09:20.072 --> 01:09:22.449
We're in room B3 right now.

01:09:23.450 --> 01:09:26.996
But the numbers on the dice are
making us split up three ways.

01:09:27.079 --> 01:09:30.749
On top of that, one of the four of us
will have to stay here.

01:09:31.333 --> 01:09:33.294
And we don't know what happened to Tetsu.

01:09:34.712 --> 01:09:38.507
He isn't in B4. So that must mean…

01:09:41.093 --> 01:09:44.263
That must mean he's in A3.

01:09:45.306 --> 01:09:46.557
Tetsu…

01:09:48.184 --> 01:09:52.396
If he's in there…
that room might deduct a lot of points.

01:09:54.732 --> 01:09:56.609
What are we supposed to do?

01:10:01.280 --> 01:10:04.366
One of you will have to go in there.

01:10:04.950 --> 01:10:09.914
Another to the confirmed minus two.
Another goes further away from the exit.

01:10:10.623 --> 01:10:14.627
And one person…
will have to choose a lockdown.

01:10:23.761 --> 01:10:25.137
Hey!

01:10:25.221 --> 01:10:28.265
Shut up, you stupid bitch!

01:10:28.349 --> 01:10:30.434
Please! 

01:10:30.517 --> 01:10:32.978
- Stop!
- Get back here! You're worthless!

01:10:33.062 --> 01:10:35.356
- Worthless! Had enough?
- Stop!

01:10:49.161 --> 01:10:50.371
Come with me.

01:10:50.454 --> 01:10:52.373
We're going to the land of death.

01:11:25.990 --> 01:11:27.533
Think of something.

01:11:30.661 --> 01:11:32.037
Think of something.

01:11:33.914 --> 01:11:35.541
Come on, think.

01:11:38.794 --> 01:11:39.962
Think.

01:12:15.873 --> 01:12:17.624
EXIT
